    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d48">

                <pb facs="0187" n="137" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv12/pg137"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf. 184.015/7</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary General of the Commission to Negotiate
                        Peace</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        Major Royall Tyler</hi><anchor n="3" xml:id="d48-f1"/></head>
                <p>1. The Commissioners on March 12th<anchor n="4" xml:id="d48-f2"/> approved the
                    sending of a mission to Esthonia, Latvia and Lithuania, under the leadership of
                    Lt. Colonel Warwick Greene, and including the following personnel: <list>
                        <item>Major Alvin Devereux, 305th F. A.</item>
                        <item>Lt. [Commander John A.] Gade, U. S. N., Naval Attaché at
                            Copenhagen.</item>
                        <item>Lt. Ludlow B. Alexander.</item>
                        <item>Lt. Ivan W. Wahren.</item>
                        <item>2nd Lt. A. H. Stonestreet.</item>
                        <item>Army Field Clerk Louis Rosenthal.</item>
                        <item>Army Field Clerk J. Holbrook [Chapman].</item>
                    </list></p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1919-03-12"><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >March</hi> 12, 1919</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d48-f1" n="3" type="source" xml:id="d48-f1-content">
                <p>Member of the Political and Economic Intelligence Section of the American
                    Commission.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d48-f2" n="4" xml:id="d48-f2-content">
                <p>See minutes of the meeting of the Commissioners Plenipotentiary, March 12, 1919,
                        <ref target="frus1919Parisv11#pg_114">vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
